## Summary

- Adds `[windows]`, `[osx]`, and `[linux]` blocks to `settings.json`.
- Applies the matching block within each configuration scope, preserving normal user/workspace/folder precedence.
- Keeps language-specific overrides independent and higher priority within the same resolved configuration.
- Adds schema completion and validation support for the platform blocks.

This allows Settings Sync to keep common settings shared while only platform-dependent values differ:

```jsonc
{
	"editor.fontSize": 16,
	"[osx]": {
		"vim.autoSwitchInputMethod.obtainIMCmd": "/opt/homebrew/bin/macism"
	},
	"[windows]": {
		"vim.autoSwitchInputMethod.obtainIMCmd": "im-select.exe"
	},
	"[linux]": {
		"vim.autoSwitchInputMethod.enable": false
	}
}
```

Profiles remain independent from the operating system, so the same workflow profile can be reused across platforms. The syntax also follows the existing platform-specific configuration precedent in `tasks.json`.

